CHUNK({"chunk":"N","module":"m4","topics":[{"id":"m4-forest-act","title":"Forest (Conservation) Act, 1980","short":"Forest Conservation Act","blurb":"Why states lost the power to divert forests, Section 2, the advisory committee, compensatory afforestation and CAMPA, the Godavarman judgment, and the 1992 and 2023 amendments.","source":"Lecture W4 (Forest and Wildlife Acts), pages 1–4","tabs":[{"title":"Background and Section 2","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">India: <b>8% of world's species</b> on <b>2.4% of land</b>. Forest Act = <b>habitat</b>, Wildlife Act = <b>inhabitants</b>.</p>\n          <p>Before 1980, <b>state governments</b> could divert forest alone (Himalayan deforestation: floods in UP, Bihar). Act moved that power to the <b>Central Government</b>.</p>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Section 2</b> (heart): no <b>non-forest use</b> or <b>de-reserving</b> without <b>prior Central approval</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>Advisory Committee</b> of experts advises the Centre.</li>\n            <li><b>Compensatory afforestation</b>: <b>equal area</b> non-forest land or <b>twice the area</b> degraded forest; funds to <b>CAMPA</b>.</li>\n          </ul>\n        "},{"title":"Judgment and amendments","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Godavarman judgment, 1996</b>: Act covers <b>all forest in the dictionary sense</b>, even if unrecorded.</li>\n            <li><b>1992 amendment</b>: transmission lines, seismic surveys, drilling, hydro projects with <b>minimal felling</b> allowed (Central approval).</li>\n            <li><b>2023 amendment</b>: renamed; coverage from <b>October 1980</b>; faster <b>border and linear projects</b>.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note trap\">Plantations are <b>not a true substitute</b> for ancient forest.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Year of the Forest (Conservation) Act?","back":"<b>1980</b>."},{"front":"Heart of the Forest Act?","back":"<b>Section 2</b>: no non-forest use of forest land without prior Central approval."},{"front":"Compensatory afforestation rule?","back":"Equal area of non-forest land, or <b>twice</b> the area of degraded forest."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m4-wildlife-act","title":"Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972","short":"Wildlife Protection Act","blurb":"The hunting and trade crisis, schedules, the ban on hunting, the protected area network, CITES, enforcement and penalties.","source":"Lecture W4 (Forest and Wildlife Acts), pages 4–6","tabs":[{"title":"Background and provisions","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Tigers <b>fewer than 2,000 by 1972</b>. Act: <b>uniform national law</b>; <b>bans</b> (not regulates) hunting; legal base for <b>Project Tiger (1973)</b>.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Schedules</b></td><td><b>Four</b> after <b>2022</b>. <b>Schedule I</b>: tiger, elephant, rhino, snow leopard, great Indian bustard</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Trade</b></td><td>Banned without ownership certificate; India's <b>CITES</b> tool</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Enforcement</b></td><td><b>Wildlife Crime Control Bureau</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Penalty</b></td><td>Schedule I: <b>3 to 7 years</b> + fine</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Protected areas and CITES","html":"\n          <div class=\"vs\">\n            <div class=\"side\"><h4>National Park</h4><p><b>No</b> human activity, no grazing.</p></div>\n            <div class=\"side\"><h4>Wildlife Sanctuary</h4><p><b>Limited</b> activity if harmless.</p></div>\n          </div>\n          <p><b>Conservation and Community Reserves</b>: <b>2002 amendment</b>. India: <b>900+ protected areas</b>, about <b>5%</b> of land.</p>\n          <p><b>CITES</b>: signed <b>1973</b>, in force <b>1975</b>, secretariat <b>Geneva</b>; India joined <b>1976</b>.</p>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Year of the Wildlife (Protection) Act?","back":"<b>1972</b>."},{"front":"Number of schedules after 2022?","back":"<b>Four</b>."},{"front":"Name Schedule I animals.","back":"Tiger, elephant, rhinoceros, snow leopard, great Indian bustard."}],"cardCount":7,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m4-forest-wildlife-together","title":"How the Forest and Wildlife Acts work together","short":"Forest and wildlife link","blurb":"Habitat and inhabitants, the 10 km rule and the National Board for Wildlife, what engineers must do, and the constitutional duty behind both laws.","source":"Lecture W4 (Forest and Wildlife Acts), pages 6–7","tabs":[{"title":"Together","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li>Projects within <b>10 km</b> of a national park or sanctuary: clearance from <b>National Board for Wildlife</b>, chaired by the <b>Prime Minister</b>.</li>\n            <li>Forest diversion near a protected area triggers <b>both Acts</b>; SC and NGT read them together.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th></th><th>Forest Act 1980</th><th>Wildlife Act 1972</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>Protects</td><td><b>Habitat</b></td><td><b>Inhabitants</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Amended</td><td>1992, 2023</td><td>2002, 2022</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"For engineers","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li>Roads, railways, power lines, dams, pipelines on forest land: <b>Forest Clearance</b>.</li>\n            <li>Near protected areas: <b>Wildlife Board approval</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>EIAs</b> must cover forest and wildlife impacts under both Acts.</li>\n            <li>Violations: <b>criminal imprisonment</b>.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <p>Constitution: <b>Article 48A</b> (State's duty), <b>Article 51A(g)</b> (citizen's fundamental duty).</p>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Distance rule for Wildlife Board clearance?","back":"Projects within <b>10 km</b> of a national park or sanctuary."},{"front":"Who chairs the National Board for Wildlife?","back":"The <b>Prime Minister</b>."},{"front":"Constitutional articles behind both Acts?","back":"<b>48A</b> (State) and <b>51A(g)</b> (citizens)."}],"cardCount":4,"formulaCount":0}],"figures":[]});
